    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34212" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pausĭas</span></b> , ae,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Παυσίας</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a celebrated
			painter</i>, <i>a native of Sicyon</i>, <i>contemporary with Apelles</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 21, 2,
				3, § 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">35, 11, 40, §
			126</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pausĭăcus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>of Pausias</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tabella,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					S. 2, 7, 95</span></i>
			.</div>
